{"availability":"available","full":"dev-formata-io/stof","name":"stof","description":"Run AI-generated logic safely, inside your app. Stof is JSON with functions: a sandboxed, embeddable runtime for Rust, JavaScript/WebAssembly, and Python.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Rust","stars":61,"forks":5,"created":"2024-12-17T22:34:06Z","updated":"2026-10-06T15:57:47Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://stof.dev","topics":["agents","ai-agents","data-format","embedded-scripting","interpreter","json-data","llm","policy-engine","python-library","rules-engine","runtimes","rust-crate","sandbox-environment","scripting-language","serialization-deserialization","serialization-format","typescript-library","webassemby"],"demo":"https://stof.dev/playground","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:21:15.684Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T13:21:15.684Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T13:21:15.684Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T13:21:15.684Z","stars":61,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Your agent can write the logic. Where do you run it?","Models are good at writing small pieces of logic: a routing rule, a validation check, a data transform, a tool. Running that logic is the hard part, because the code came from a model, not from your team.","Stof is the missing option: a small language made to be written by models, sent as data, and run in-process in a sandbox."],"features":["Safe by default. A document can only read and change itself and call the functions you give it.","Fast and in-process. No containers or cold starts: parsing and running a small document takes under a millisecond, and each call after that takes microseconds.","Small on the wire. Documents, functions included, serialize to compact binary: the rules above are under 1KB.","It starts as JSON. Any JSON document is valid Stof, and Stof imports and exports JSON, YAML, TOML, and more.","Models already write it. Stof reads like JSON, so models write it without a lot of special training, and errors give the exact line and a plain explanation, so a model can fix its own mistakes."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dev-formata-io/stof/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f737a3d5917d0a5f713e401b80914170b4567b8f5b0ecd49b6ebe474e506c9ed","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T13:21:15.832Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:21:15.832Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Your agent can write the logic. Where do you run it?","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dev-formata-io/stof/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f737a3d5917d0a5f713e401b80914170b4567b8f5b0ecd49b6ebe474e506c9ed","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dev-formata-io/stof/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T13:21:15.832Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-06T15:57:47Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dev-formata-io/stof/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T13:21:15.833Z","hash":"f737a3d5917d0a5f713e401b80914170b4567b8f5b0ecd49b6ebe474e506c9ed","originalBytes":11441,"storedBytes":11441,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["stof","run","model","json","logic","data","document","functions","app","await","documents","give","like","triage","doc","runtime","write","access","call","models","python","rules","rust","typescript","allow","already","code","default","file","language","own","runs","small","system","them","total","units","where","add","browser","const","doc.parse","errors","graph","hello","http","inside","let","line","only","read","running","same","toml","tool","webassembly","when","wrote","yaml","api","container","doc.call","else","everything","formata","host","import","imports","install","it.","itself","javascript","library","mistakes.","new","nothing","notify","one","part","plain","reach","rule","self.ticket.team","starts","stofdoc.new","test","text","under","why","agent","any","billing","binaries","binary","cargo","ch